# Telegraft

[![Telegraft Orchestration Framework](https://dl.dropbox.com/s/rs05ps3ipx5y3yt/telegraft.jpg?dl=1)](http://binocarlos.github.com/telegraft/)

Minimalistic orchestration manager for [node](http://nodejs.org). [![Build Status](https://secure.travis-ci.org/binocarlos/telegraft.png)](http://travis-ci.org/binocarlos/telegraft)

```js
var telegraft = require('telegraft');
var broadcast = telegraft();

// make our recording
broadcast.record(function(){

	// announce a scene
	broadcast.announce('Getting uptime for all servers');

	// actually do something
	broadcast.transmit(function(transmission){
		transmission.modulate('ssh', 'uptime');
	});

	// wait for all servers to finish
	broadcast.wait();

	// trigger another recording when ready
	broadcast.record(telegraft.recordings.service({
		name:'httpd',
		action:'restart'
	});

})

// send out the above recording to some servers
broadcast.initiate([
	'server1.mydomain.com',
	'server2.mydomain.com',
	'...',
	'server297.mydomain.com'
]);

```

## Installation

    $ npm install telegraft

## Features

  * Manage simultenous sequences of commands across hundreds of servers
  * Healthy library of recording functions (like user, service, file, package etc)
  * Functional architecture - infrastructure as (JavaScript) code

## Philosophy

  Telegraft exists to orchestrate complicated sequences of commands that are sent to 
  multiple (simultenous) targets.

  It exists to make the job of distributed server configruation simple.

## Running Tests

To run the test suite first invoke the following command within the repo, installing the development dependencies:

    $ npm install

then run the tests:

    $ make test

